4. Those who consume more than 25 g of alcohol per day on average within three months before signing the informed consent form (for example, 750 mL of beer, 250 mL of wine, or 50 mL of Baijiu), or cannot stop using any alcoholic products during the study period, or those who are positive in the alcohol breath test during screening;
5. Drug abusers, or those who have tested positive for urinary drug abuse during screening, including: morphine, methamphetamine, ketamine, cocaine, ecstasy (dimethylenedioxoamphetamine), marijuana (tetrahydrocannabidiol acid);
