详细说明:
Evaluations will include:

1. Quantification of disease activity through standardized clinical scores;
2. Standardized ultrasound examination of 10 index joints;
3. Ophthalmological examination with slit lamp and search for inflammatory cells in the anterior segment with optical coherence tomography(OCT);
4. Collection of blood, urine, tears, and, in the case of joint infiltration, synovial fluid (SF) samples for carrying out the following analyses:

* Evaluation of routine hematologic laboratory parameters and known markers of disease activity
* Whole exome sequencing (WGS) on patients and families to identify any predisposing genetic factors
* Multiomic analyses (proteomic, metabolomic, and lipidomic)
* Immunological characterization: leukocyte subset imunophenotyping, cytokine/chemokine profiling, NETosis quantification
* Extracellular-vesicle analysis: miRNomic, proteomic, and phenotypic characterization

Primary Objective:

To evaluate the safety and tolerability following single and multiple oral dministrations of TUL321 capsules in healthy participants.

Secondary Objectives:

1. To characterize the pharmacokinetic (PK) profiles following single and multiple oral administrations of TUL321 capsules in healthy participants;
2. To evaluate the effect of a high-fat meal on the PK profiles after a single oral administration of TUL321 capsules in healthy participants;
3. To preliminarily assess the in vivo biotransformation and mass balance characteristics following single oral administration of TUL321 capsules;
4. To characterize the pharmacodynamic (PD) profiles following single and multiple oral administrations of TUL321 capsules in healthy participants;
5. To evaluate the effect of single oral administration of TUL321 capsules on the QT/QTc interval.

